From 87c5804c58d62559e5edb52a13d330a0dde6ed8c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?=C3=98yvind=20Harboe?= <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 19:53:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] sdc: deleting an instance from an exception is linear, not
 quadratic
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Deleting a pin, instance or net goes through Sdc::editExceptions, which
unrecorded and re-recorded every exception naming the object in full:
its first point index and its pin index, walking every object of every
point. With the common block constraint

  set_max_delay -from [all_inputs] -to [all_registers]
  set_max_delay -from [all_registers] -to [all_outputs]

each exception names every register, so deleting registers one at a
time, as dead logic elimination does, costs the number of deleted
registers times the number of registers.

A removal only takes an object out of the points: the index entries of
every object that stays are unchanged, and the callers already erase
the removed object's own keys. editExceptions takes whether the edit is
a removal; a removal records the merge hashes again (the points hash as
a whole, incrementally) and leaves the indices alone. An exception
whose -through holds pin pairs derived from its objects is recorded
again in full, since those pairs are keyed by pins the callers do not
erase, as is every edit that moves constraints to another object.

Deleting all but one of N registers under the two constraints above:

      N   before    after
   2000    4.2 s   0.12 s
   4000   17.2 s   0.25 s
   8000   75.5 s   0.52 s
  16000  348.0 s   1.06 s

sdc_delete_exception_insts deletes instances from -from, -to and
-through exceptions one at a time and checks that the paths of the
instances that remain keep the slacks they had, and that an exception
left with no instance is deleted. A removal that drops the remaining
instances' index entries fails it (no path from the remaining
registers).

Upstream: The-OpenROAD-Project/OpenSTA#482 (draft). Carried in
bazel-orfs; retires on the //:bump onto an OpenROAD whose OpenSTA has it.

Signed-off-by: Øyvind Harboe <oyvind.harboe@zylin.com>
---
